  planner_response {
    response: "I have designed and implemented the **S.A.G.E. Landing Page**:\n\n### 1. Platform Purpose & Overview\n- **Clear & Fearless Identity**: Explains S.A.G.E. in simple, accessible language as a secure, anonymous campus grievance and escalation platform that gives students a voice to report hostel, mess, hygiene, WiFi, and safety concerns without risk of academic or administrative retribution.\n- **Direct Call-to-Action Controls**: Prominent dual action buttons (**\"Submit a Complaint\"** and **\"Browse Complaints\"** with live counter badge) linking directly into the submission workflow and public ledger.\n\n### 2. Privacy & Security Architecture\n- **Encrypted & Hidden by Default**: Outlines zero-knowledge privacy guarantees \342\200\224 no sign-in or student credentials required, no IP/device tracking, and zero identity metadata committed with grievances.\n- **Audited Misuse Safeguards**: Reassures students that reveal options exist strictly for verified extreme criminal offenses (e.g., violent extortion, bomb threats) requiring dual-signoff from university proctorial and legal boards, with every single query permanently recorded to a public audit log.\n- **Anti-Retaliation Protection**: Proctors, professors, and contractors only see the factual description and location, removing fears of grading or hostel penalties.\n\n### 3. Comparison: S.A.G.E. vs. The Physical Suggestion Box\n- **Side-by-Side Architectural Contrast**:\n  - *Status Tracking*: Replaces unmonitored paper drop-boxes with real-time status progression (`Submitted` \342\206\222 `Under Review` \342\206\222 `Resolved`).\n  - *Prioritization*: Replaces subjective review with community upvoting to amplify urgent, widespread hostel failures.\n  - *Accountability*: Replaces one-way silence with transparent official administrative remarks and technician dispatch notes.\n  - *Safety*: Eliminates camera and handwriting concerns with client-side decoupled digital submission.\n\n### 4. 3-Step Lifecycle & Interactive FAQ\n- **Visual 3-Step Workflow**: Quick reference detailing *1. Submit Anonymously*, *2. Community Upvotes*, and *3. Action & Public Notes*.\n- **Interactive FAQ Accordion**:\n  - *\"Is this really anonymous?\"*\n  - *\"What happens after I submit?\"*\n  - *\"How does anonymity work, and is there any exception?\"*\n  - *\"How does upvoting help my issue get resolved faster?\"*\n  - *\"Can professors or hostel wardens see who complained about them?\"*\n- **Universal Navigation**: Seamlessly accessible via the top navigation bar (`How It Works`), the masthead brand logo, and the footer."
    modified_response: "I have designed and implemented the **S.A.G.E. Landing Page**:\n\n### 1. Platform Purpose & Overview\n- **Clear & Fearless Identity**: Explains S.A.G.E. in simple, accessible language as a secure, anonymous campus grievance and escalation platform that gives students a voice to report hostel, mess, hygiene, WiFi, and safety concerns without risk of academic or administrative retribution.\n- **Direct Call-to-Action Controls**: Prominent dual action buttons (**\"Submit a Complaint\"** and **\"Browse Complaints\"** with live counter badge) linking directly into the submission workflow and public ledger.\n\n### 2. Privacy & Security Architecture\n- **Encrypted & Hidden by Default**: Outlines zero-knowledge privacy guarantees \342\200\224 no sign-in or student credentials required, no IP/device tracking, and zero identity metadata committed with grievances.\n- **Audited Misuse Safeguards**: Reassures students that reveal options exist strictly for verified extreme criminal offenses (e.g., violent extortion, bomb threats) requiring dual-signoff from university proctorial and legal boards, with every single query permanently recorded to a public audit log.\n- **Anti-Retaliation Protection**: Proctors, professors, and contractors only see the factual description and location, removing fears of grading or hostel penalties.\n\n### 3. Comparison: S.A.G.E. vs. The Physical Suggestion Box\n- **Side-by-Side Architectural Contrast**:\n  - *Status Tracking*: Replaces unmonitored paper drop-boxes with real-time status progression (`Submitted` \342\206\222 `Under Review` \342\206\222 `Resolved`).\n  - *Prioritization*: Replaces subjective review with community upvoting to amplify urgent, widespread hostel failures.\n  - *Accountability*: Replaces one-way silence with transparent official administrative remarks and technician dispatch notes.\n  - *Safety*: Eliminates camera and handwriting concerns with client-side decoupled digital submission.\n\n### 4. 3-Step Lifecycle & Interactive FAQ\n- **Visual 3-Step Workflow**: Quick reference detailing *1. Submit Anonymously*, *2. Community Upvotes*, and *3. Action & Public Notes*.\n- **Interactive FAQ Accordion**:\n  - *\"Is this really anonymous?\"*\n  - *\"What happens after I submit?\"*\n  - *\"How does anonymity work, and is there any exception?\"*\n  - *\"How does upvoting help my issue get resolved faster?\"*\n  - *\"Can professors or hostel wardens see who complained about them?\"*\n- **Universal Navigation**: Seamlessly accessible via the top navigation bar (`How It Works`), the masthead brand logo, and the footer."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
